{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user is asking me to implement a `solve(case)` function for a Toolformer API-call filtering task. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. For each call: compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens)\n3. A call is accepted if: parseable == True AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics in original order\n\nThe key properties mentioned:\n- `normalized_weights`: normalize by prediction tokens\n- `stronger_counterfactual`: use the stronger counterfactual (loss_without - loss_with)\n- `inclusive_threshold`: \u003e= threshold (not \u003e)\n- `stable_order`: maintain source order\n\nLet me think about the output format. The function should return:\n- accepted call IDs\n- rounded per-call diagnostics\n\nLooking at the fixture data, I need to figure out what \"rounded\" means - probably round to some decimal places.\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import math\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    required_call_fields = {\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"}\n    \n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: calls\")\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        for field in required_call_fields:\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field in call: {field}\")\n        if call[\"prediction_tokens\"] \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call['call_id']}\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        # Accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"gain\": round(gain, 6),\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 6),\n            \"parseable\": parseable,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics,\n        \"total_accepted\": len(accepted_ids)\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- call0: gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445, norm = 1.18778445/5 = 0.23755689, parseable=True → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, norm = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=True → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, norm = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=True → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, norm = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=True → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, norm = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=True → accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, norm = 1.09421604/4 = 0.27355401, parseable=False → NOT accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call4\n\nThe response must be a JSON object with a single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source code as a string.\n\nLet me write the complete implementation cleanly:\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    required_fields = {\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"}\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        missing = required_fields - set(call.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call at index {i} missing fields: {missing}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"], (int, float)) or call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"] \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call['call_id']}\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # stronger counterfactual: gain from having the call\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        # normalize by prediction token count\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        # inclusive threshold: \u003e= threshold; also requires parseability\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"gain\\\": round(gain, 8),\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\\n            \\\"parseable\\\": bool(parseable),\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_ids,\\n        \\\"total_accepted\\\": len(accepted_ids),\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01bVAQFOwGYXZRAmnkB3lyrw","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2047},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2047,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":34,"output_tokens":1586,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1056},"service_tier":"standard"}}